atlas capability

architecture command-law
  canonical_name CommandLawGraph
  family capability
  domain Capability / Computational Law
  layer capability
  semantic_question What computational law does this command preserve, beneath its domain?
  purpose The second axis of the estate, from the run6/run7 deep read: the 91 commands are faces of a few deep calculi -- composition, causal execution, coupled dynamics, evidence/evolution -- plus the multi-identity laws (hash/canon/graph/family/entity). Domain says what estate; law says what algebra a hop preserves, which is what makes composition sound.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Command
  node_types Law
  edge_types preserves_law
  internal_calculus law classification (composition / causal / coupled / evidence-evolution / representation / retrieval / media / governance)
  invariant a command's law is what a composed hop must preserve; the estate is what it belongs to
  forbidden_inference same domain -> same law
  forbidden_inference a law label -> a proof the algebra holds
  command BonfyreDiscipl
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/command_laws.py
  source_path 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/command_advertisements.py
  witness 10-Code/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_command_advertisements.py
  publishes CommandAdvertisement
  known_gap the whole 91-cmd surface (94 dirs, 87 built) is advertised as CommandAdvertisements mapped to the capability each provides (BonfyreAuth->Authority, BonfyreLedger->Value, BonfyreFPQ->FPQRepresentation, ...) and served in the fabric; binding each advertisement's consumes/produces into DisCIPL composition is the next step
  interacts capability-lattice
  interacts discipl-composition
  source_lineage run6/run7 second deep read -- 91 commands as deep calculi
